#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-03.png", width: 5pt), 221.5pt, 233pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(294.65pt, 803.976pt, "3 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 82.32pt, "SPP-induced SHG can be employed as a surface probe of buried interfaces, resolving simultaneously ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 101.3pt, "the challenge of weak and localized SHG signals and thus enabling measurements in fields including ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 120.26pt, "material and surface research for energy, catalysis and others. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 158.18pt, "Main ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 196.22pt, "Surface plasmon polaritons are optical excitation that travel along an interface between a materials with ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 215.18pt, "a negative real part of relative permittivity (typically a metal) and a dielectric [30]. SPPs can propagate ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 236.9pt, "significant distances (~ 200 µm ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(221.69pt, 230.42pt, "1")
  #line-at(221.69pt, 242.42pt, "𝑒")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(226.37pt, 236.9pt, " amplitude decay length on a gold-air interface at 1030 nm, the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 259.22pt, "wavelength relevant for this study) on flat metal surfaces provided the intrinsic Ohmic losses are ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 278.21pt, "sufficiently low [31,32]. SPPs, being evanescent surface waves, do not directly couple to the optical ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 297.29pt, "beams incident from the surroundings due to momentum mismatch, so their excitation is typically ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 316.25pt, "achieved via Kretschmann-type configuration")
  #line-at(281.81pt, 316.25pt, "or through employing a grating to provide additional ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 335.21pt, "momentum to the incident beam [30]. We employed the latter approach and used focused ion beam ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 354.17pt, "(FIB) milling to fabricate gratings for SPP excitation on a large {111}-surface of a thick (> 1 µm) ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 373.13pt, "monocrystalline gold flake (see Methods for synthesis and fabrication details [33]).  ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 411.05pt, "A schematic of the initially studied system is presented in Figure 1a: an incident pulsed laser beam is ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 430.01pt, "focused on an in-coupling grating, exciting an SPP that travels on the gold surface and is then out-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 448.97pt, "coupled from an identical grating at 30 µm distance. The geometrical parameters of the grating were ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 468.07pt, "optimized for the operational wavelength of the laser – 1030nm, with details described in the Methods ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 487.03pt, "section, and optical image of the sample is shown in Figure 1b. As shown in Figure 1c, the gratings ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 505.99pt, "function as expected: illumination of the in-coupling grating (bright spot on the left-hand side) results ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 524.95pt, "in a visible signal at the out-coupling grating (two stripes on the right-hand side). We also carried out ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 543.91pt, "absorption measurements which suggest up to 20 % of the incident power couples to a surface-plasmon-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 562.87pt, "polariton, as discussed in Supplementary Information Note 1.  ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 600.79pt, "We subsequently measured SHG from the same sample, shown in Figure 1d on a logarithmic scale. We ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 619.75pt, "confirmed the observed signal was SHG through both its spectrum and quadratic scaling with incident ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 638.83pt, "fundamental laser beam power (Supplementary Information Note 2). As expected, strong SHG is ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 657.82pt, "observed at a location coinciding with the excitation laser spot, due to the strong nearfields in the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 676.78pt, "vicinity of the abrupt surface discontinuities at the grating. A weaker SHG signal is also clearly seen at ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 695.74pt, "the outcoupling grating, i.e. the signal is delocalized with respect to the excitation position, with total ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 714.7pt, "counts 0.5 % of the intensity of the SHG at the excitation spot, which can be clearly seen in a line profile ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 733.66pt, "presented in Figure 1e.  Importantly, this plot also reveals that no SHG signal was detected from the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 752.616pt, "planar gold surface between the gratings:  overlaying the white light reflection clearly demonstrates that ")
]

