#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-27.png", width: 450.5pt), 72pt, 180.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(294.65pt, 803.976pt, "9 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 82.32pt, "Supporting Information Note 7 – oscillations observed from monocrystalline surfaces")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 103.94pt, "We regularly observed oscillations in the SHG signal from flat surfaces. This was always a small ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 123.02pt, "component of the total signal, typically less than 20 %. To investigate this further we present the back-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 141.98pt, "focal-plane measurements shown in Figure S5c")
  #line-at(285.89pt, 141.98pt, "on a log scale in Figure S7a. Small SHG components ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 160.94pt, "are present at higher angles (similar to that observed in other SHG experiments [5]).  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 386.45pt, "Figure S7. a) Equivalent of Figure S5c, but on a logarithmic scale. Dashed black line indicates ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 405.41pt, "approximate maximum extent of the back-focal plane. b) Schematic of the interference of two plane ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 424.61pt, "waves incident on a detector, with one plane wave incident at an angle ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(386.71pt, 424.61pt, "𝜃")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(393.19pt, 424.61pt, " to the detector plane. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 451.73pt, "We recorded the spacing of the real space oscillations, which did not correspond to the wavelength of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 470.71pt, "the SPP nor a frequency doubled SPP. Rather, we find that the spacing of the fringes is 0.78 µm for NA ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 489.67pt, "of 0.7, but changes with objective NA (0.64 µm/1.13 µm for NA of 0.75/0.45). We consider two plane ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 508.63pt, "waves incident on our detector, one perpendicular to the detector and one incident at a high angle, as ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 527.59pt, "we recorded in Figure S7a (see schematic, Figure S7b). These plane waves will introduce an ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 546.67pt, "interference pattern on the detector. The measured spacing of the fringes (i.e. ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(409.63pt, 546.67pt, "𝑎")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(415.99pt, 546.67pt, " on Figure S7b) matched ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 565.99pt, "that observed when the high angle wave is incident with the maximum angle (NA) allowed by our ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 584.95pt, "objective, confirming that the real-space oscillations are due to the interaction of these two plane waves. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 603.91pt, "This is further demonstrated in Figure S8")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(254.93pt, 603.91pt, ": ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(261.65pt, 603.91pt, "here we close an iris in the back-focal-plane and record the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 622.87pt, "real-space image. As the range of incident angles is reduced, the spacing of the oscillations reduces i.e. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 641.83pt, "there is a small background SHG component at several angles, and the highest angle component ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 660.82pt, "produces the oscillations that we observe. We also note that our back-focal-plane results are fully ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 679.78pt, "consistent with taking a Fourier transform of the real space images. ")
]

